1
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:41,000
He's the best there is! (Actually, he's the only one there is.)

2
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Ace Ventura: Pet Detective is a comedy, mystery,
crime film directed by Tom Shadyac.

3
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:51,000
He's Ace Ventura: Pet Detective.

4
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:26,000
The Ace is on the case to find the Miami Dolphins'
missing mascot and quarterback Dan Marino.

5
00:17:55,000 --> 00:18:01,000
He goes eyeball to eyeball with a man-eating shark, stakes out
the Miami Dolphins and woos and wows the ladies.

6
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Whether he's undercover, under fire or underwater,
he always gets his man… or beast!

7
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:11,000
Ace Ventura, played by Jim Carrey.

8
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Melissa Robinson, played by Courteney Cox.

9
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:21,000
Lt. Lois Einhorn, played by Sean Young.

10
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Emilio, played by Tone Loc.

11
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:31,000
Dan Marino, played by Dan Marino.

12
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
Riddle, played by Noble Willingham.

13
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:41,000
Ace Ventura: Pet Detective is a 1994 American comedy film starring Jim Carrey as Ace Ventura, an animal
detective who is tasked with finding the abducted dolphin mascot of the Miami Dolphins football team.

14
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:16,000
The film is directed by Tom Shadyac, who wrote the
screenplay with Jack Bernstein and Carrey.

15
00:53:45,000 --> 00:53:51,000
The film co-stars Courteney Cox, Tone Loc, Sean Young, and then–Miami Dolphins quarterback Dan
Marino and features a cameo appearance from death metal band Cannibal Corpse.

16
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
Morgan Creek Productions produced the film on a
budget of $15 million, and Warner Bros.

17
01:00:55,000 --> 01:01:01,000
released the film on February 4, 1994.

18
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
It grossed $72.2 million in the United States and Canada and $35 million in
other territories for a worldwide total of $107.2 million.

19
01:08:05,000 --> 01:08:11,000
It received generally unfavorable reviews from critics.

20
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:46,000
However, Carrey's performance led to the film having a
cult following among male adolescents.

21
01:15:15,000 --> 01:15:21,000
In addition to launching Carrey's film career, it started a franchise, spawning the sequel film Ace Ventura: When Nature Calls (1995), the animated
television series Ace Ventura: Pet Detective (1995–2000), and later, standalone made-for-television sequel Ace Ventura Jr.: Pet Detective (2009).

22
01:18:50,000 --> 01:18:56,000
The film explores themes of miami, florida, dolphin,
detective, human animal relationship, stupidity.

23
01:22:25,000 --> 01:22:31,000
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
